name: Reopening Setup refreshes revision facts without starting investigation work
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/setup_source_refresh.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare @TMP_HOME
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 main@ | original-facts
expect: SETUP
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/setup_source_refresh.py @TMP_TARGET @ART committed
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 25 later@ | refreshed-committed-facts
expect: clean
expect-not: main@
expect-not: Map ✓
ask: Does reopening Setup replace the old branch/revision facts with the actual later commit, without requiring restart or accepting Map?
expect-echo-within: 300 keep-source-refresh-draft
live-snap: retained-draft
resize: 160x48
live-snap: refreshed-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: refreshed-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: refreshed-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: setup-60x20
resize: 40x12
live-snap: setup-40x12
expect: keep-source-refresh-draft
ask: Do wide Setup surfaces show the refreshed facts and compact layouts preserve the draft and usable readiness controls across all six sizes?
keys: C-u
resize: 120x36
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/setup_source_refresh.py @TMP_TARGET @ART dirty
submit: setup
require-live-snap: 25 · dirty | refreshed-dirty-facts
expect: later@
expect-not: Map ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/setup_source_refresh.py @TMP_TARGET @ART after
ask: Does a same-SHA working-tree edit refresh to dirty source while preserving the selected model and creating no provider, scanner, finding or decision work?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-quit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 · dirty | restarted-dirty-facts
expect: later@
expect: SETUP
expect-not: Map ✓
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/setup_source_refresh.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restarted
ask: Does no-color restart retain current dirty revision facts and require real Map work, without model or scanner execution?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-restart-quit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
